{\qc
Chapter 1\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {\s2 \afs28
{\b
{\i
{\qc
The Murder That Hadn't Happened Yet\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At precisely 9:17 on a Tuesday morning, Derek Gent received an email informing him that he was dead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was not particularly surprised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had always suspected that death would arrive by email.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not because he was especially pessimistic, but because nearly everything important seemed to arrive by email these days. Electricity bills. Insurance renewals. Invitations to webinars. Notifications that someone had changed a password Derek had never used.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Death was simply the logical next step.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What surprised him was the sender.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The message had come from the Derek Gent Relativistic Investigation Bureau.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek stared at the screen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Bureau was not supposed to send him emails.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was his Bureau.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
More precisely, it was a small private investigative organization occupying two rooms on the second floor of an old office building in London, plus a corridor which the landlord insisted was a communal area and Derek insisted belonged to the Bureau whenever he needed somewhere to put a coat.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Bureau dealt primarily with unusual cases.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was partly because Derek liked unusual cases and partly because ordinary cases paid terribly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sign on the frosted glass door read:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
DEREK GENT RELATIVISTIC INVESTIGATION BUREAU\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Underneath, in smaller letters:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
CAUSALITY, CHRONOLOGY & OTHER INCONVENIENCES\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And underneath that, added by Penny Gent several years earlier:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
NO MURDERS BEFORE 10 A.M. WITHOUT AN APPOINTMENT\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had objected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent had pointed out that they had never actually received a murder before ten.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had said that this was beside the point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent had said that was precisely the point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had lost.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was now looking at an email from the Bureau.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The subject line was:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
CASE UPDATE: DEREK GENT\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He opened it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dear Mr Gent,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
We regret to inform you that you have been murdered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The incident will occur tomorrow at 11:03 a.m.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The perpetrator has been identified.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It is you.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kind regards,\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek Gent Relativistic Investigation Bureau\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek read it again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then a third time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked at the sender's address.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was correct.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked at the Bureau's computer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was his computer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked around the office.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everything appeared to be where it ought to be.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The filing cabinet was locked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The kettle was where the kettle normally was, which was not necessarily where it ought to be.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The window was shut.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The door was shut.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing appeared to have been disturbed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at the email again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
