The Rain, the Underground and the Problem with Poetry\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek Gent had been given a difficult assignment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was to investigate the London Underground on rainy days.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This was not, in itself, unusual.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The London Underground was already difficult on most days.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
On rainy days it became something else entirely.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
People arrived wet, irritated and vaguely convinced that the entire transport system had been personally designed to inconvenience them. Trains became late. Platforms became slippery. Umbrellas became weapons. Shoes acquired the consistency of soup.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had been instructed to find out whether anything in the Underground, specifically on rainy days, could prevent Special Relativity and General Relativity from both being true at the same time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had read the instruction three times.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he had called Weinstein.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alfred."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you aware that you've sent me to investigate the London Underground?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"On rainy days."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"To determine whether it contains something that makes Special Relativity and General Relativity mutually incompatible."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek paused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, that's settled."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"One question."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein had been silent for several seconds.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he had said:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because time doesn't exist."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had waited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's your explanation?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not quite."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What is the rest?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein had sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm beginning to suspect that time is a bookkeeping device."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Like accounting?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That sounds dangerous."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It is."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And the Underground?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Also dangerous."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had considered this.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Anything else?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rain."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Right."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And that was how, at 4:18 on a wet Thursday afternoon, Derek Gent found himself standing on a London Underground platform with a notebook in one pocket, a train ticket in the other, and an increasingly damp left shoe.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked up at the station sign.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked at the rainwater dripping from the entrance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He looked at the arriving train.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he looked at his notebook.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At the top of the page he had written:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
INVESTIGATION 1047-B\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Underneath:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
QUESTION:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Can London Underground infrastructure, under rainy conditions, prevent SR and GR from simultaneously describing reality?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Under that he had written:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
SECONDARY QUESTION:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And underneath that:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
THIRD QUESTION:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
What the hell does poetry have to do with it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek closed the notebook.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A woman standing beside him glanced at the page.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She looked at him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then at the page.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then back at him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Work?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Unfortunately."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She smiled sympathetically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Important?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Apparently."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
She stepped onto the train.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek followed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The train doors closed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The carriage moved.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek sat down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Across from him, a man was reading a newspaper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The headline concerned the weather.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then at the rain running down the window.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then at his notebook.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He opened it again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wrote:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Start with SR.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Special Relativity was not difficult in principle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two observers in relative inertial motion could assign different coordinates to the same event.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time intervals and spatial intervals could differ between frames.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The speed of light remained invariant.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Lorentz transformation connected the descriptions.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing about that contradicted ordinary experience.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It merely contradicted the assumption that everyone was entitled to the same clock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
General Relativity went further.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gravity was not merely a force acting across space.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Spacetime itself had geometry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Matter and energy influenced that geometry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Freely falling objects followed geodesics.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clocks followed worldlines and measured proper time along them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Again, nothing inherently contradictory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Indeed, General Relativity contained Special Relativity locally.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In sufficiently small regions of spacetime, where curvature could be neglected, freely falling observers recovered the familiar rules of SR.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek stopped writing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was the obvious answer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
SR and GR weren't enemies.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
GR contained SR as its local limit.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So why had Weinstein sent him into the Underground?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at the wet floor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
