{\qc
The Open-Door Principle\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was a rule at the Bureau.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was not written down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It did not appear in the employee handbook.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was, in fact, no employee handbook, largely because Derek considered employee handbooks "a form of administrative poetry."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nevertheless, everyone knew the rule.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If an office door was open, the occupant had vanished into virtuality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Obviously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no point knocking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no point calling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no point standing in the doorway shouting someone's name.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
An open office door meant that the person in question had ceased, for all practical purposes, to occupy ordinary spacetime.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might be in another room.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might be in London.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might be in Munich.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might be in a completely different reference frame.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They might even, on occasion, be dead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Bureau had learned not to worry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If the door was closed, however, the situation was entirely different.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then the person was in there.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Obviously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They were either working hard...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
...or shafting, equally hard.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no third possibility worth discussing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek had first formulated the principle after Penny Gent had disappeared for three hours.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had found her office door open.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had checked the kitchen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had checked the laboratory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had checked the basement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He had checked the train timetable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Eventually he had returned to her office.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The door was still open.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor had appeared beside him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where's Penny Gent?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Virtuality."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Right."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They went back to work.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
