"Because their frames of reference differ."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He drew light cones.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The speed of light defines the causal structure."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor looked at the diagram.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If two events are inside one another's light cones..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They can be causally connected."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And everyone agrees on their causal order."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But if they're outside one another's light cones..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They're spacelike separated."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And different observers can disagree about which happened first."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That explains the train."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Potentially."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why potentially?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because our train is also moving through curved spacetime."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So General Relativity matters."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And then the coordinates can become even stranger."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent pointed at the newspaper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So the headline could appear before the article that caused it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not quite."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because information cannot travel outside the causal structure."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So no actual message from the future."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Correct."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Just a strange coordinate description."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's reassuring."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek folded the newspaper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Never be reassured too early."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They stood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The train had disappeared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was no record of it on the station board.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No destination.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No arrival.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No departure.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor looked at Derek.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where did it go?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at the rails.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I don't know."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's a first."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek ignored her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He crouched beside the track.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was something on the rail.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A small brass plate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He picked it up.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was engraved with a single number:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
11:17\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor stared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent looked at the plate.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Perhaps 11:17 isn't a time."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at her.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What else could it be?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"An event."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek went very still.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent continued.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Something happens at 11:17."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But perhaps the clocks aren't telling us when it happens."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek nodded slowly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"They're identifying it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor looked between them.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So 11:17 is an event label."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Maybe."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then when the geometry changes, the labels become misleading."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked toward the tunnel.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Which means we've been asking the wrong question."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor sighed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Again?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Again."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They stood silently for a moment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then Derek looked at the sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The rain had stopped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was unusual.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Very unusual.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Penny Gent noticed it too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"London has stopped raining."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor looked upward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's worse than the train."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Much worse."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A single drop of water fell from the sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It stopped halfway down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then moved upward.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then sideways.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then disappeared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"General Relativity."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor frowned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you sure?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Derek looked at him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, that's settled."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And somewhere beneath them, the train that had never officially existed began its journey again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to one clock, it had already arrived.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to another, it had not yet departed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to the railway timetable, it had never existed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Which, Derek thought, was probably the most reliable information of all.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {\page } {\s1 \afs32
