"Good."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A tensor can describe relationships involving several directions at once. Scalars have no directional components. Vectors have one directional character. Tensors generalise this idea and, crucially, have well-defined transformation rules when we change coordinates."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Trevor nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So the components can change while the physical object doesn't."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
