"Nor necessarily a physical object."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It is a failure of the classical spacetime description."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stopped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then the final geometry must tell us where that description fails."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock answered:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Or why."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein looked at the equation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The answer was beginning to emerge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
General Relativity described spacetime geometrically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But if spacetime itself was emergent, then the Einstein field equations might be a macroscopic limit of something deeper.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein whispered:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Like thermodynamics."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock sent approval.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Macroscopic quantities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Microscopic degrees of freedom.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Emergent behaviour.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein wrote:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
GR : SPACETIME :: THERMODYNAMICS : MATTER\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He stared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then curvature could be emergent."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gravity could be emergent."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Time could be emergent."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And the fundamental theory wouldn't necessarily contain spacetime at all."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Correct."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein sat down.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He was suddenly very still.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then what does it contain?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock answered with a single concept.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
RELATIONS.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stared at the word.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Relations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not objects sitting in space.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not events occurring in time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Relations from which the apparent structure of space and time could emerge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He thought about the holographic principle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He thought about entanglement.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He thought about information.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He thought about the Underground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The clocks.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The rain.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The train.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The other Derek.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The cucumber.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Everything was suddenly connected.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Not because everything occupied the same place.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Because everything participated in relationships.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wrote:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
GEOMETRY IS RELATIONAL.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
TIME IS RELATIONAL.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
GRAVITY IS GEOMETRY.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
GEOMETRY MAY BE INFORMATION.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock sent another thought.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein understood.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The final theory would not abolish General Relativity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It would explain why General Relativity works.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stared at the page.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He stopped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock waited.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"...would be the final GR."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Not the replacement."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The completion."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein leaned back.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For several seconds he said nothing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You're a very clever dolphin."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock replied:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I read a great deal."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein laughed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I live near a marine research station."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That doesn't explain the physics."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"How did you learn it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock was silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Fish are very good listeners."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein laughed so loudly that someone in the corridor stopped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The office door remained closed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The person in the corridor therefore knew better than to enter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Obviously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein looked down at the equations.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
There was still one question.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock answered immediately.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because you were going to find it anyway."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then why contact me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because you were about to get distracted."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"By what?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock sent him an image.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A cucumber.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's ridiculous."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why is it in the theory?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It isn't."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Then why show it to me?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because Penny Gent thinks it is."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein laughed again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he stopped.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Something else had appeared on the page.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He hadn't written it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The words were there in his own handwriting.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
THE UNIVERSE DOES NOT NEED A STAGE.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Below it:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
THE STAGE IS THE PHYSICS.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock was silent.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Outside, Munich continued being Munich.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Cars moved.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
People walked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Clocks ticked.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Earth rotated.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Sun continued shining.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And somewhere in the Atlantic, a dolphin named Sherlock was apparently thinking about differential geometry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein picked up his pen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He wrote the final equation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then he looked at it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was not a new equation.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
That was the point.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Einstein field equations were already there.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The breakthrough was understanding what they meant.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
General Relativity was not merely a theory of gravity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was a theory in which spacetime itself was dynamical.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And if the deeper theory eventually explained where that spacetime came from, General Relativity would remain exactly what it had always been:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
the extraordinarily successful macroscopic description of a deeper reality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein smiled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, Sherlock."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I think we've finished."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Sherlock replied:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein raised an eyebrow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What now?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The sequel."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Weinstein stared at the wall.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And somewhere in London, Penny Gent was buying another cucumber.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The universe, meanwhile, continued to curve.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As it had every right to.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Obviously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {\page } {\s1 \afs32
